  "description": "SignalR's programming model over a Windows named pipe.\n\nWrite a Hub, get Clients.All / Clients.Group / Clients.Caller and IHubContext on the server; build a HubConnection with On/SendAsync/InvokeAsync, automatic reconnect and Closed/Reconnecting/Reconnected on the client. The wire format is SignalR's JSON hub protocol — record-separated JSON frames, the same message types — but the transport is a named pipe, so there is no HTTP server, no port to open and no URL to configure.\n\nIntended for processes on one machine that need to talk to each other: a tray app and the applications it configures, a service and its console, an IDE extension and a debuggee.",
